{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0432","billNumberShort":"H.B. 432","billNumberLong":"HB0432","fileNumber":"2026FL0979","shortTitle":"Egg Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"SHIPPRP","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Shipp, Rex P.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"STRATKJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Stratton, Keven J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses eggs.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines and modifies terms;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies fee and rulemaking authority for the Department of Agriculture and Food (department) regarding the distribution, sale, and inspection of shell eggs;<hr><ltbullet>establishes that a person may not:<hr><ltbullet1>distribute shell eggs unless the person obtains a license from the department; or<hr><ltbullet1>sell shell eggs from a small producer outside of the state;<hr><ltbullet>requires a large egg producer to register with the department as a food establishment;<hr><ltbullet>clarifies the requirements for small and large egg producers; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Ryan C. Williams","fiscalAnalyst":"Lacey K. Moore","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"RNLMPHBIMH","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 09:25:19.323","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 09:25:19.327","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill assigned to staff for fiscal analys